RuOS: double-press power launches MIR Pay instead of the camera.

Inserts one call into GestureLauncherService.handleCameraGesture(): if MIR Pay is
installed, RuosPowerGesture.launchMirPay() launches it and we return before the stock
camera path runs. If MIR Pay is absent it returns false and the camera gesture
behaves normally.

The helper it calls lives at
  frameworks/base/services/core/java/com/android/server/ruos/RuosPowerGesture.java
(placed in the tree by tools/integrate_into_aosp.sh) and compiles as part of the
globbed services sources — no Android.bp change needed.

Apply from the AOSP root (context-matched, tolerant of line drift):
    patch -p1 --fuzz=3 < vendor/ruos/patches/gesture-launcher-mirpay.patch

If it still won't apply (method refactored in your revision), make the change by hand:
in handleCameraGesture(), immediately BEFORE the line
    StatusBarManagerInternal service = LocalServices.getService(
insert:
    if (com.android.server.ruos.RuosPowerGesture.launchMirPay(mContext)) {
        return;
    }

--- a/frameworks/base/services/core/java/com/android/server/GestureLauncherService.java
+++ b/frameworks/base/services/core/java/com/android/server/GestureLauncherService.java
@@ -1,9 +1,14 @@
             if (useWakelock) {
                 // Make sure we don't sleep too early
                 mWakeLock.acquire(500);
             }
+            // RuOS: double-press power launches MIR Pay instead of the camera.
+            if (com.android.server.ruos.RuosPowerGesture.launchMirPay(mContext)) {
+                return;
+            }
             StatusBarManagerInternal service = LocalServices.getService(
                     StatusBarManagerInternal.class);
             service.onCameraLaunchGestureDetected(source);
         } finally {
             Trace.endSection();
         }
